On Oct 7, 2:39=A0am, Patric Mueller <bh...@bigfoot.com> wrote:
> Some UnNetHack user found a smallish bug that also exists in Vanilla.
>
> First clean a level of all items, then go into a vault and wait for
> the vault guard to appear.
>
> Kill the vault guard and then quaff a potion of object detection.
>
> You will get the message "You sense the presence of objects" even
> though none are shown and also the guard's inventory cannot be found
> anywhere by digging.
>
> I don't know yet what is causing this behavior.

     I haven't investigated this, but can guess what is probably
happening, or at least part of it.  When a vault guard is killed
or sent way, he actually gets moved to invalid map coordinate <0,0>
and stays there until his temporary corridor to/from the vault
gets removed.  Once that's gone, then he's finally discarded.

     If he's kept artificially alive--I think he might be--then he
won't be skipped by the various monster scanning loops.  But he
still ought to drop everything he was carrying at the time he got
killed, so shouldn't have any inventory for detection to notice.
Something may be getting done in the wrong order and accidentally
interfering with that.

     The vault stuff is "arcane", to put it politely, and always
seems to be a hassle to deal with....


